1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,702
Version zero of CloudCart is built,

2
00:00:02,702 --> 00:00:03,268
deployed,

3
00:00:03,268 --> 00:00:03,897
and fixed.

4
00:00:03,897 --> 00:00:05,218
But can you prove it?

5
00:00:05,218 --> 00:00:06,728
Not on your own machine,

6
00:00:06,728 --> 00:00:08,993
with files left over from last week.

7
00:00:08,993 --> 00:00:09,559
Prove it,

8
00:00:09,559 --> 00:00:10,377
from nothing.

9
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,865
Today is the mastery lesson.

10
00:00:12,865 --> 00:00:16,326
One scenario that anyone can check: a clean clone,

11
00:00:16,326 --> 00:00:16,880
a build,

12
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,503
a deploy,

13
00:00:17,503 --> 00:00:18,680
a customer check,

14
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,095
a tag,

15
00:00:19,095 --> 00:00:20,549
and written evidence.

16
00:00:21,099 --> 00:00:23,595
If every step passes from a fresh copy,

17
00:00:23,595 --> 00:00:24,939
version zero is real.

18
00:00:24,939 --> 00:00:25,771
If one fails,

19
00:00:25,771 --> 00:00:28,075
you found a problem that was hiding.

20
00:00:28,625 --> 00:00:31,099
Clone it, build it, deploy it, check it, tag it.

21
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:35,721
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

22
00:00:36,271 --> 00:00:40,218
One: you clone the project fresh. Nothing is left over from before.

23
00:00:40,768 --> 00:00:44,330
Two: you build it with Maven, and deploy the war you just built.

24
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,848
Three: you check it like a customer, then tag the exact commit you built.

25
00:00:49,398 --> 00:00:54,625
Four: you write four lines of evidence. Then your turn, with a lab that judges all of it.

26
00:00:55,175 --> 00:01:00,999
This lesson closes the CloudCart version zero project. Five lessons, one app, proven.

27
00:01:01,549 --> 00:01:03,810
Clone, build, deploy, check, tag, prove.

28
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:09,295
One scenario, six steps, and every step has a witness.

29
00:01:09,845 --> 00:01:13,770
A clean clone. The witness: git status says nothing is changed.

30
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:18,928
A build. The witness: Maven's own count of passing tests, and a war file.

31
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:24,150
A deploy and a customer check. The witness: the health page, and the product list.

32
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,740
A tag and four lines of evidence.

33
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,347
The witnesses: the commit,

34
00:01:28,347 --> 00:01:29,274
the test count,

35
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:30,572
the file fingerprint,

36
00:01:30,572 --> 00:01:31,313
the version.

37
00:01:31,863 --> 00:01:32,895
If a step fails,

38
00:01:32,895 --> 00:01:36,054
you use the method from the last lesson: symptom,

39
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:36,634
evidence,

40
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:37,021
cause,

41
00:01:37,021 --> 00:01:37,279
fix,

42
00:01:37,279 --> 00:01:37,666
proof.

43
00:01:39,216 --> 00:01:44,357
Go to the lab folder.

44
00:01:45,907 --> 00:01:47,806
Look around. Type: L S.

45
00:01:48,356 --> 00:01:49,407
Tomcat is here,

46
00:01:49,407 --> 00:01:49,827
empty.

47
00:01:49,827 --> 00:01:51,158
And origin.git,

48
00:01:51,158 --> 00:01:52,558
the team repository.

49
00:01:52,558 --> 00:01:55,780
We do not have the project on our machine yet.

50
00:01:56,330 --> 00:02:01,599
Clone the project.

51
00:02:02,149 --> 00:02:02,902
One command,

52
00:02:02,902 --> 00:02:04,785
and the whole project is here,

53
00:02:04,785 --> 00:02:05,852
with its history.

54
00:02:05,852 --> 00:02:08,613
This is how every engineer starts on a team.

55
00:02:09,163 --> 00:02:11,339
Go inside. Type: CD, work.

56
00:02:11,889 --> 00:02:13,959
Is the copy clean?

57
00:02:14,709 --> 00:02:19,402
Main, matching origin main, and no changed files. A clean starting point.

58
00:02:19,952 --> 00:02:22,235
What are we about to build?

59
00:02:22,985 --> 00:02:25,311
One commit: CloudCart version zero.

60
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,171
A short code in front of it.

61
00:02:27,171 --> 00:02:28,434
Remember that code.

62
00:02:28,434 --> 00:02:30,959
It is the exact version we will build,

63
00:02:30,959 --> 00:02:31,225
tag,

64
00:02:31,225 --> 00:02:32,222
and write down.

65
00:02:32,772 --> 00:02:39,471
Build it, and keep the test summary.

66
00:02:48,021 --> 00:02:49,578
Maven compiled the code,

67
00:02:49,578 --> 00:02:50,486
ran the tests,

68
00:02:50,486 --> 00:02:51,719
and packed the war.

69
00:02:51,719 --> 00:02:53,081
Thirty-two tests run,

70
00:02:53,081 --> 00:02:53,860
no failures,

71
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:54,508
no errors.

72
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:56,001
That count is evidence,

73
00:02:56,001 --> 00:02:57,493
so remember thirty-two.

74
00:02:58,043 --> 00:03:01,819
Is the war there?

75
00:03:02,369 --> 00:03:06,529
About three hundred thousand bytes. The war you built, from a clean clone.

76
00:03:07,079 --> 00:03:15,185
Deploy it into Tomcat.

77
00:03:15,735 --> 00:03:32,717
Start Tomcat, then ask right away.

78
00:03:36,267 --> 00:03:38,438
Symptom: curl could not connect.

79
00:03:38,438 --> 00:03:41,898
The evidence: nothing is listening on the port yet.

80
00:03:41,898 --> 00:03:45,087
The cause: Tomcat needs a few seconds to start,

81
00:03:45,087 --> 00:03:46,376
and unpack the war.

82
00:03:46,376 --> 00:03:47,665
The fix is to wait,

83
00:03:47,665 --> 00:03:48,683
then ask again.

84
00:03:49,233 --> 00:04:00,305
Wait, then ask again.

85
00:04:06,855 --> 00:04:12,231
Status up, version zero point two point oh. The proof: asked again, as a customer.

86
00:04:12,781 --> 00:04:24,706
Count the products.

87
00:04:25,256 --> 00:04:29,587
Twelve products. The catalog is complete, so the customer check passes.

88
00:04:30,137 --> 00:04:35,043
Tag the commit.

89
00:04:35,593 --> 00:04:40,372
A tag is a permanent name for one exact commit. No output means it worked.

90
00:04:40,922 --> 00:04:44,421
Publish the tag.

91
00:04:44,971 --> 00:04:50,496
New tag, pushed to the team repository. Now everyone can find exactly this version.

92
00:04:51,046 --> 00:05:06,214
Write the evidence. First, the commit.

93
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:15,425
The test count.

94
00:05:15,975 --> 00:05:31,655
The file fingerprint.

95
00:05:32,205 --> 00:05:41,741
The version.

96
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:46,494
Read it back.

97
00:05:47,044 --> 00:05:47,733
Four lines.

98
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:48,421
The commit,

99
00:05:48,421 --> 00:05:49,486
thirty-two tests,

100
00:05:49,486 --> 00:05:51,051
a fingerprint of the war,

101
00:05:51,051 --> 00:05:52,053
and the version.

102
00:05:52,053 --> 00:05:53,681
Anyone can check each one,

103
00:05:53,681 --> 00:05:54,745
and the lab will.

104
00:05:55,295 --> 00:05:57,663
Run the judge.

105
00:05:58,213 --> 00:05:59,030
Five checks,

106
00:05:59,030 --> 00:05:59,848
five passes.

107
00:05:59,848 --> 00:06:00,801
A clean clone,

108
00:06:00,801 --> 00:06:01,686
a real build,

109
00:06:01,686 --> 00:06:03,184
the right war running,

110
00:06:03,184 --> 00:06:03,593
a tag,

111
00:06:03,593 --> 00:06:04,955
and honest evidence.

112
00:06:05,505 --> 00:06:07,467
Clean up.

113
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:10,385
Tomcat stopped, and everything removed.

114
00:06:10,935 --> 00:06:15,607
Is the port free? Count the lines.

115
00:06:16,157 --> 00:06:20,957
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind. Version zero is proven.

116
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:25,366
Your task. Prove version zero, from a clean clone.

117
00:06:25,916 --> 00:06:30,353
One: lab up. Clone the team repository into a folder called work.

118
00:06:30,903 --> 00:06:35,020
Two: build it with Maven, and deploy the war you built into Tomcat.

119
00:06:35,570 --> 00:06:37,227
Three: ask the health page,

120
00:06:37,227 --> 00:06:38,209
like a customer.

121
00:06:38,209 --> 00:06:39,559
If it does not answer,

122
00:06:39,559 --> 00:06:41,032
use the incident method.

123
00:06:41,582 --> 00:06:45,806
Four: tag the commit, cloudcart-v0, and push the tag.

124
00:06:46,356 --> 00:06:51,113
Five: write evidence.txt, four lines. Then lab check, and lab down.

125
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:55,040
Here is where to find everything.

126
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,576
This is the mastery lesson,

127
00:06:56,576 --> 00:06:58,966
so pause on this screen and write it down.

128
00:06:59,516 --> 00:07:01,164
The lab lives on GitHub,

129
00:07:01,164 --> 00:07:02,331
at it-waves,

130
00:07:02,331 --> 00:07:03,910
/devops-ai,

131
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:05,421
in the folder academy,

132
00:07:05,421 --> 00:07:06,108
/lab.

133
00:07:06,658 --> 00:07:12,375
Two files: lab117.sh, and shortcuts117.sh.

134
00:07:12,925 --> 00:07:13,834
Install it,

135
00:07:13,834 --> 00:07:16,726
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

136
00:07:16,726 --> 00:07:18,626
- m seven five five,

137
00:07:18,626 --> 00:07:20,775
lab117.sh,

138
00:07:20,775 --> 00:07:22,014
into /usr

139
00:07:22,014 --> 00:07:23,005
/local

140
00:07:23,005 --> 00:07:23,997
/sbin.

141
00:07:24,547 --> 00:07:29,774
Load the short name with: source shortcuts117.sh. You get: lab.

142
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:31,507
You need a JDK,

143
00:07:31,507 --> 00:07:31,924
Maven,

144
00:07:31,924 --> 00:07:32,203
git,

145
00:07:32,203 --> 00:07:32,551
curl,

146
00:07:32,551 --> 00:07:34,151
unzip and the ss tool.

147
00:07:34,151 --> 00:07:36,169
About one gigabyte of memory,

148
00:07:36,169 --> 00:07:41,250
and ports 8089 and 8099 free.

149
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:42,989
The lab downloads Tomcat,

150
00:07:42,989 --> 00:07:44,103
and the project,

151
00:07:44,103 --> 00:07:44,660
for you.

152
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:46,917
Lab up prepares everything.

153
00:07:46,917 --> 00:07:48,624
Lab check judges your work.

154
00:07:48,624 --> 00:07:50,141
Lab down removes it all.

155
00:07:50,141 --> 00:07:52,164
Only run it on your own machine.

156
00:07:54,214 --> 00:07:56,283
Pass or fail. You need all five.

157
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:59,969
Your work folder is a clean clone, at the latest commit.

158
00:08:00,519 --> 00:08:03,143
It was built: a valid war, and the tests ran.

159
00:08:03,693 --> 00:08:06,381
Tomcat runs the war you built, and health is up.

160
00:08:06,931 --> 00:08:09,534
Origin has the tag, on the commit you built.

161
00:08:10,084 --> 00:08:11,940
Your four lines of evidence match.

162
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:13,791
To pass, all five.

163
00:08:15,841 --> 00:08:17,612
Your turn, on your own machine.

164
00:08:18,162 --> 00:08:22,066
One: lab up, read the task list, and clone the project into work.

165
00:08:22,616 --> 00:08:25,432
Two: build with Maven, and read the test summary.

166
00:08:25,982 --> 00:08:29,672
Three: deploy the war, start Tomcat, and wait before you ask.

167
00:08:30,222 --> 00:08:33,785
Four: check the health page and the products, then tag and push.

168
00:08:34,335 --> 00:08:39,476
Five: write the four evidence lines, and run lab check until you see five out of five.

169
00:08:40,026 --> 00:08:42,608
Six: lab down, and prove the port is free.

170
00:08:43,158 --> 00:08:44,992
Pause the video, and begin now.

171
00:09:00,542 --> 00:09:01,417
Quick check.

172
00:09:01,967 --> 00:09:04,036
Why do we prove a build from a clean clone?

173
00:09:04,586 --> 00:09:07,103
What does a git tag give you that a branch does not?

174
00:09:07,653 --> 00:09:09,637
Which four facts make up the evidence?

175
00:09:10,187 --> 00:09:12,747
What do you do when the health page does not answer?

176
00:09:13,297 --> 00:09:16,256
Objective covered: CloudCart version zero,

177
00:09:16,256 --> 00:09:17,453
mastery evidence.

178
00:09:17,453 --> 00:09:18,862
A verified scenario,

179
00:09:18,862 --> 00:09:20,623
its results written down,

180
00:09:20,623 --> 00:09:21,468
and cleanup.

181
00:09:22,018 --> 00:09:24,087
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

182
00:09:34,637 --> 00:09:38,328
Next: web servers, with nginx in front of CloudCart.

183
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:42,206
